---
description: No dangerous actions without approval
alwaysApply: true
---

Never do these without explicit user approval:
- Send a mainnet transaction.
- Deploy to mainnet.
- Use a real private key.
- Print or expose secrets.
- Delete project files.
- Drop or truncate databases.
- Run destructive migrations.
- Run sudo.
- Install global system tools.
- Modify OS-level configuration.
- Push to remote Git repository.
- Change production config.
- Disable security checks.

When a command may be dangerous, explain the risk and ask for approval first.

For local development, prefer Docker Compose and project-local tools.
